# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[sparkling|Sparkling]]; [[fizzy]].
#: {{co|en|'''brisk''' cider}}
# Stimulating or invigorating.
#: {{ux|en|This morning was a '''brisk''' fall day. It wasn't cold enough for frost, but you wanted to keep moving.}}
# Abrupt, curt in one's manner or in relation to others.
#: {{ux|en|The service in that restaurant was '''brisk''' and impersonal.}}
#* {{RQ:Maugham Moon and Sixpence|[[s:The Moon and Sixpence/Chapter XV|chapter 15]]||Her '''manner''' was brisk, and her good-breeding scarcely concealed her conviction that if you were not a soldier you might as well be a [[counterjumper|counter-jumper]].}}

